.bench-tmp/
.bin/
# Everything the cross-language subjects compile goes to `.bench-tmp/` by way of
# CARGO_TARGET_DIR and -Dbench.target, and the Maven repository to `.bin/m2`.
# These two catch a manual `cargo build` or `mvn package` run by hand in place.
servers/rust/target/
servers/java/target/
# `results/*`, not `results/`: git cannot re-include a path inside an excluded
# directory, and the one published run has to be tracked. The docs site renders
# it, and CI builds that site from a clean checkout - an untracked report means
# the deployed page has no numbers on it.
results/*
!results/latest.json
# `logging.json` is tracked for the same reason: `src/logging-tables.ts` renders the
# README's "Request logging cost" section from it, and a checkout without it would
# regenerate that section as "no run recorded".
!results/logging.json
